# fw_printenv and fw_setenv configuration
#
# The env is the first 128 KB of GPT p1 (LBA 32768), addressed through the
# whole disk because that is how fwup writes it (UBOOT_ENV_OFFSET, O_DIRECT).
# Linux keeps a separate page cache per block device, so reading through
# /dev/rootdisk0p1 could return a stale env after an fwup write.
# scripts/check-env-config.sh checks these numbers against fwup and U-Boot.

# Device name		Device offset	Env. size
/dev/rootdisk0		0x1000000	0x20000
